Your Contribution
Protostatix, a division of Englobe, is looking for their next Senior Structural Engineer. For nearly four decades, Protostatix has been a leader in Western Canada in the structural engineering field. As a Senior Structural Engineer you will work in direct collaboration with the project team: in this role, a highly collaborative work style is imperative, design/detailing will not be performed in isolation, but in a team-based manner.
Your Main Responsibilities Will Be:
Function relatively independently as the lead design engineer while working in conjunction with the structural engineering technologists on staff to generate working drawings, as well as other project team members (including intermediate engineering staff at our firm, the project architect, other engineering subdisciplines and the project contractor).
Perform analysis and design of structural elements utilizing variety of materials including concrete, steel, masonry, light-gauge metal, wood and pre-cast using the latest applicable building code and standards;
Oversee the generation of deliverable documentation (ie. drawings and specifications) for structural projects which requires accuracy in calculations and/or completeness of data;
Production of structural review reports and technical reviews both of new and existing structures
Assist in contract administration and technical review of site issues during construction
Interact directly with clients and actively promote business development opportunities
Apply and promote Englobe's health and safety rules
Your Profile
Must have a currently valid P.Eng (Professional Engineer) seal with APEGA, or equivalent provincial association (e.g.: PEO, EGBC, APEGS, etc.)
Must hold a minimum Master's degree from a recognized post-secondary facility with focus on structural engineering;
Preference given to Candidates with Ph.D or post-doctoral background, and candidates with British Columbia 'Designated Structural Engineer' (Struct.Eng.) designation)
Must have a minimum of 10 years of experience in the design and detailing of built structures in concentrations such as multi-family residential, commercial, light industrial or institutional structure types. This may include design of greenfield, ground-up structures, or maybe include the analysis/renovation of existing structures;
Strong preference shall be given to candidates with multi-storey concrete/high-rise design expertise
The ideal candidate has past experience working with lateral/seismic forces;
Experience working with pertinent finite element design packages, such as SAFE, ETABS and SFRAME is considered an asset;
Must have background managing design teams and be comfortable working with junior engineers or engineers-in-training and other team members in a mentorship role as necessary
Candidate must display familiarity with pertinent Canadian design codes, including but not limited to: CSA A23.1/2 and A23.3, CSA S16 and pertinent ACI publications. Familiarity designing with the National Building Code of Canada (NBCC) and being up-to-date on current iterations of the code is critical;
Ability to meet tight deadlines and work under pressure; and
Demonstrated sensitivity and consideration for occupational health and safety.
